    "lastSynced": "2026-07-10",
    "lastSyncNotes": [
      "Full re-audit via figma.variables API (previous version had drift/typos from an earlier manual pass).",
      "Added missing 'cherry-on-cherry' and 'cherry-plus' to Light neutrals.",
      "Added entirely missing 'error' and 'success' semantic color collections.",
      "Removed 'grey' and 'light-grey' from Dark neutrals: these are not B2B design-system variables (legacy palette leftovers, not present in this Figma file).",
      "Corrected value typos: cherry-disabled, yellow-hover*, soda-disabled, cherry-brighter, cream-white (see git history for old values).",
      "Rebuilt spacing scale to match the real 'Universal Sizes' Figma collection (2,4,8,12,14,16,18,22,24,26,28,32,40,44,48,56,80,120): old scale (1,6,10,20,64) did not exist in Figma.",
      "Rebuilt borderRadius and stroke to use the real Figma variable names (Micro/XSmall/Small/Medium/Regular/Large/XLarge) instead of invented xs/sm/md/lg/xl aliases. There is no 'full/pill' radius token in Figma: pill shapes use an arbitrary large px value, not a token.",
      "Typography is now split by breakpoint. The Figma 'Typography' collection has three MODES: Desktop / Tablet / Mobile: and every heading/body size has a distinct value per mode. Previous version only captured one flat scale and did not reflect this.",
      "Added 'breakpoint' block from the 'Device size' Figma collection (Mobile 375 / Large mobile 640 / Tablet 820 / Desktop 1440 / Large desktop 2560)."
    ]
